            <ArticleTitle>Essential Elements of a Collaborative Mental Health Training Program for Primary Care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>839-850</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1056-4993(17)30083-4</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.chc.2017.06.012</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mental health integration in primary care is based on creating an environment that encourages collaboration and supports appropriate care for patients and families while offering a full range of services. Training programs for primary care practitioners should include sessions on how to build and maintain such a practice along with information on basic mental health competencies.</AbstractText>
